**`ErrorBoundary.tsx`** — usage:

```tsx
// Basic
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary fallback={<p>Oops!</p>}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// With error callback (e.g. Sentry)
<ErrorBoundary onError={(err, info) => Sentry.captureException(err)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

**Key details:**
- `getDerivedStateFromError` triggers the fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` logs to console + calls optional `onError` prop
- Retry resets state, causing children to remount
- `role="alert"` for screen reader accessibility
- Must be a class component — hooks can't catch render errors
